From: Hang(Harry) Gao <GaohRyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:51:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] opt: reset sampler uses horizon-normalised return-to-go
 for episodes that end without failure (clip_end_norm)

The return-binned sampler read 'few steps left before the clip end' as 'hard': in the sim2real-dr run the last two
bins of each clip (0.9% of frames) received 40.5% of all resets and truly hard clips got no extra weight.
With --env.sampler-clip-end-norm the return-to-go of episodes that end by clip end or time-out is rescaled by
1/(1-gamma^remaining); steps with fewer than 25 remaining steps are dropped; failed episodes are unchanged.
